{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "29cf38a1-41e6-8a3c-b7c7-9faa32c53613",
  "created_at": "2026-03-09T11:13:15-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Neusa Rocha",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priya Raman",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:08:08-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Priya. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:08:13-04:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah. I got a late fee on my water and sewer bill and I'm not happy about it, because I mailed that check on time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:08:24-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I can look into that. Can I get the service address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:08:30-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "184 Gibbs Avenue. Ocean Drive side. The name on it is Neusa Rocha."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:08:36-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Ms. Rocha. Let me pull that up. Do you have the bill in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:08:44-04:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I do, I'm looking right at it. It says the due date was February twenty-seventh. And then there's a late charge line down at the bottom."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:08:55-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And when did you mail the payment?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:08:59-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The Monday before. February twenty-third. I put it in the mailbox at the end of my street. I remember because I was on my way out, and I said to myself, okay, that's done."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:09:13-04:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. Let me look at the account. [pause] I'm showing the payment posted on March second, which is after the due date, so the late charge was applied automatically."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:09:26-04:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "March second. See, that's what I don't get. I called last week and the woman said, it probably got held up in the mail. And I said, well, that's not my fault, I mailed it a week early. And she said she couldn't remove it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:09:45-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. A payment mailed by the due date can still arrive late, and the system goes by the date we receive it. But there is a way to ask for a review."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:09:59-04:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so how do I dispute it formally? Because a phone call to somebody who says she can't do anything isn't really it for me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:10:10-04:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. You'd send a written request to the billing office. Include your name, the service address, the account number from the bill, the amount of the late charge, and the date you mailed the check. If you have your bank statement showing the check number, or a cancelled check, attach a copy."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:10:32-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The check hasn't come back yet, but the number is in my checkbook. I can send that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:10:40-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That helps. Also, is the check number written on the payment stub you sent in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:10:47-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think so. I usually write it on the memo line. Not on the stub though, no."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:10:55-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine, just put it in your letter. A supervisor reviews these, and they'll decide whether to adjust the charge."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:11:04-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And where do I send it? Is there an address, or do I email it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:11:11-04:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The mailing address for the billing office is printed on your bill, near the remittance section. Look for the line that says to send correspondence. You can also drop a letter off at the counter at City Hall during business hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:11:28-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, it's on the back, I see it. I'll mail it, but this time I'm going to pay attention to the postmark, I guess. I told my husband, I said, I'm never trusting that mailbox again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:11:43-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand the frustration. If you mail it certified, you'll have a receipt for the date it went out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:11:51-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine. Is there a deadline for the dispute?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:11:55-04:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd send it as soon as you can. The sooner it's in, the sooner it's reviewed. I'll also add a note to the account now that you've called, so the reviewer sees that you raised it today."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:12:11-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. Will the late fee stay on the bill while they decide? Because I don't want it to turn into another charge."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:12:21-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll note the dispute on the account. Because it's under review, you can pay the base amount, and the review would address the late charge. I can't promise the outcome, but the note will be there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:12:36-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. That's something. I've got to go, I'm actually standing in line at the post office right now. I'm returning a sweater, it was a size too small."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:12:48-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, while you're there, you could ask about certified mail for your letter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:12:54-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I might just do that, actually. Okay. So letter, account number, check number, the dates, certified. Got it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:13:02-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. Anything else I can help with today?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:13:07-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's it. Thanks for your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-09T11:13:11-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Ms. Rocha. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
